<main class="sheet">
    <%- partial("layouts/top", {"here": "demo"}) %>

    <section class="hero">
        <div class="mark">Demo<span>&sect;08</span></div>
        <div>
            <h1>The gallery, running in this page.</h1>
            <p class="lede">
                Below is the same client that the download links give you, compiled to
                WebAssembly and drawing on a <code>&lt;canvas&gt;</code>. The picture you
                see before you press anything is a real render too &mdash; taken off the
                wire by the repository's <code>snapshot</code> tool, not a mockup &mdash;
                so a browser that cannot run the client still shows you the application.
            </p>

            <p>
                It is a <strong>viewing vehicle and not the model</strong>. The browser
                supplies three things and nothing else: a GPU surface, a socket and a
                pointer. There is no DOM below that line, no HTML, no CSS and no cascade
                &mdash; the module is the client, and the server sends only data. What it
                costs is a two-megabyte download the native client does not, which is why
                nothing is fetched until you ask for it.
            </p>

            <figure class="demo" data-eui data-component="gallery" style="margin:0">
                <div class="demo__stage">
                    <img class="demo__poster"
                         src="/images/demo/gallery-light.png"
                         data-light="/images/demo/gallery-light.png"
                         data-dark="/images/demo/gallery-dark.png"
                         width="1800" height="1350"
                         alt="Meridian: a dashboard with revenue, orders, open invoices, a quarter target and a work list."
                         loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                    <canvas class="demo__canvas" id="eui-gallery" tabindex="0"
                            aria-label="A live EUI session: the gallery" hidden></canvas>
                    <button class="demo__run" type="button">Run it <small>&asymp;2 MB</small></button>
                    <p class="demo__note" role="status" hidden></p>
                </div>
            </figure>

            <p>
                The session is opened on <em>this</em> host and not on the demo server's,
                because Soli refuses a WebSocket upgrade whose <code>Origin</code> is not
                its own &mdash; a page and the session it opens have to share an origin.
                The proxy makes that true by routing <code>/_eui/</code> here to the
                application that answers it.
            </p>

            <p>
                One thing you will notice: the gallery's <strong>Scene</strong> pane is
                empty here, and that is the design rather than a fault. A node whose
                capability was not granted draws its own background and nothing else
                (<a href="/docs/security">08 &sect;3</a>) &mdash; and this page grants
                nothing at all, so no reader is ever asked for anything. Even if it did,
                <code>scene</code> is not offered in a browser: WebGPU reports a shader's
                validation errors asynchronously, so the client cannot say whether a
                module the <em>server</em> wrote compiled until after it has been used,
                and a capability that cannot be checked is not one to grant. Open the
                same application in the native client to see that pane draw.
            </p>

            <p>
                Everything else it gives up is written down rather than glossed:
                the publisher key and TLS are the browser's here rather than the client's,
                the decoder does not get a process of its own, and <code>scene</code> is
                not offered at all &mdash; WebGPU reports a shader's validation errors
                asynchronously, so a browser cannot say whether a module the server wrote
                compiled until after it has been used.
            </p>

            <p>
                <a href="/samples">Eight applications rendered by the native client</a>,
                or <a href="https://eui-data.solisoft.net/live/counter">five of them running
                on the demo server</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>

<%# The browser client's bootstrap, and the only JavaScript on this site
    beyond the fifteen lines that light up a paragraph when you hover a byte.
    Five kilobytes, and it fetches nothing until the button is pressed.

    The version is the one `xtask-web` stamped into the manifest beside the
    module, carried on the URL because the module is served `immutable` for a
    year — right for bytes that never change, fatal for bytes that do. It
    lives in this view rather than the layout because this is the one page
    with a session on it. %>
<script type="module" src="<%= "/eui/eui-embed.js?v=" + eui_build %>"></script>
